Synchronized output (DEC private mode 2026) from mosh-client.

mosh-client writes each frame to the local terminal in one write, but the
terminal may read and draw a large one in several pieces. Bracketing every
frame with CSI ? 2026 h and CSI ? 2026 l makes a terminal that knows the mode
(Ghostty, kitty, WezTerm, iTerm2, tmux, ...) show it whole. A terminal that
doesn't know it ignores the private mode.

Client side only, and independent of 0006.

diff --git a/src/frontend/stmclient.cc b/src/frontend/stmclient.cc
index 1e259f4..5dba978 100644
--- a/src/frontend/stmclient.cc
+++ b/src/frontend/stmclient.cc
@@ -287,7 +287,13 @@ void STMClient::output_new_frame( void )
 
   /* calculate minimal difference from where we are */
   const std::string diff( display.new_frame( !repaint_requested, local_framebuffer, new_state ) );
-  swrite( STDOUT_FILENO, diff.data(), diff.size() );
+  if ( !diff.empty() ) {
+    /* One frame, drawn whole: bracketed as synchronized output (DEC private mode 2026), the
+       local terminal shows it all at once even when it reads the frame in several pieces.
+       A terminal without the mode ignores the brackets. */
+    const std::string frame = "\033[?2026h" + diff + "\033[?2026l";
+    swrite( STDOUT_FILENO, frame.data(), frame.size() );
+  }
 
   repaint_requested = false;
 
